+
+# Post cover images use the attachments layer
+
+## Context
+
+Authors want an optional cover image per post, shown on the post page and in
+the list. Uploads are bytes a stranger chose: they must never land under
+`public/` (served as-is), a refused file must leave no post, row or file
+behind, and replacing, removing or deleting a cover must delete its file.
+
+## Decision
+
+Use the framework's attachments layer (`bunx guren add attachments`) instead
+of a hand-rolled upload table and route:
+
+- `Post` is `Attachable` with `cover: hasOneAttached({ image: 'require' })`.
+  `attach()` on a has-one collection purges the previous row and file, so a
+  replacement never leaves the old file behind; `detach()` handles the
+  "remove cover" checkbox; `purgeAttachments()` runs before the post row is
+  deleted (no FK cascade reaches `attachments`).
+- Files go on the private `local` disk under `storage/app` (test runs use
+  `storage/app/testing`) and are served back through the signed delivery
+  route, which is why `coverUrl` is a signed, expiring URL rather than a
+  static path.
+- The app's own rule (PNG or JPEG, at most 2 MB) lives in
+  `validateCoverUpload()` and runs before any row is written, throwing a
+  `ValidationException` on the `cover` key so the response is the same 422
+  a blank title produces. The engine's own decode is the second line of
+  defence against a mislabelled file.
+- `posts.update` takes an optional `removeCover` field that is `'1'` from a
+  multipart form and a boolean when Inertia sends JSON.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Every page that renders posts loads covers with `Post.withAttachments()`
+  and reads `coverUrl` from `PostResource`; new listings must do the same
+  or `coverUrl` is `null`.
+- `Post` is registered in `Model.morphMap` so `attachments:prune` can verify
+  orphaned rows; `storage/` is gitignored.
+- Delivery URLs expire, so pages should render `coverUrl` at request time,
+  not cache it.
